# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# apps/chatbot environment configuration
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in ONE provider key. `.env.local` is
# git-ignored and read only at server startup — restart `yarn dev` after editing.
#
# The model provider is chosen by which key is present (first match wins):
#   1. GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY  → Google Gemini   (recommended, free, no card)
#   2. GROQ_API_KEY                  → Groq            (free fallback, no card)
#   3. ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL + _API_KEY → Anthropic-compatible gateway (local dev)
# Set just one. If several are set, the first in that order wins.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Option 1: Google Gemini (recommended deploy path) ────────────────────────
# Free key from Google AI Studio (https://aistudio.google.com/apikey), no credit card.
GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=

# ── Option 2: Groq (free fallback) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Free key from the Groq console (https://console.groq.com/keys), no credit card.
# Note: the 8K-TPM free tier is tight for this tool-heavy bot; prefer Gemini.
GROQ_API_KEY=

# ── Option 3: Anthropic-compatible gateway (local dev) ───────────────────────
# e.g. a local SAP Hyperspace "Hai" proxy. The SDK posts to ${ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL}/messages.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is sent as `Authorization: Bearer …` and is required when BASE_URL is set.
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=http://localhost:6655/anthropic/v1
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ── Model id override (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Blank falls back to the provider default:
#   Google    → gemini-3.5-flash   (avoid gemini-3.8-flash / gemini-flash-latest: often 503-throttled)
#   Groq      → qwen/qwen3.8-27b
#   Anthropic → claude-sonnet-4-5
# Other verified-working Gemini ids: gemini-3.7-flash, gemini-3.6-flash, gemini-3.5-flash-lite
CHAT_MODEL=

# ── MCP endpoint (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The MCP server the chat route connects to. Blank → this app's own route.
# MCP_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:3000/api/mcp
